{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/httpdestinations"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","type":"reference"},{"text":" is a destination that posts each batch it receives as the requests its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":" splits it into: one request for an endpoint without limits. Each body is whatever","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the encoder writes for its records, so events need no ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"text":" conformance and the wire format is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"yours. It sends with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"text":" through","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport","type":"reference"},{"text":" by default, or through any ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","type":"reference"},{"text":" you pass.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A send that gets no response, or a 5xx, 408 or 429 status, is sent again after the next wait of its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff","type":"reference"},{"text":": 1 second, doubling up to 60 seconds, unless you pass another. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination takes the next batch only once this one is delivered or dropped, so a tracker’s store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps the batch’s records until then. A batch the endpoint answers with any other status, whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request can never be sent, or that the encoder can’t encode is dropped, logged and reported on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports","type":"reference"},{"text":" as an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport","type":"reference"},{"text":", as is each record the encoder leaves out","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of its requests. So is a request still undelivered at its ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest\/deadline","type":"reference"},{"text":", which an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoder sets for a vendor that misdates or ignores old events: the destination checks it on its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"now:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" clock before every attempt and sends nothing more once it has passed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The tracing instrument injects the trace context of each request’s first record into its header","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fields, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Content-Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is always the encoder’s.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reach for this module to send to a server whose format you write yourself. For TraffluentCollector’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format,